HexTruncatedSeriesMathlib Phase 3 conformance was reviewed. The library is a
proof-only correspondence layer with no executable reifier, certificate
checker, tactic, or other runtime surface, so the absence of a dedicated
Conformance module and HexConformance glob is intentional.

The transported representation, ring operations, truncation, powers of X,
derivative, inverse, substitution, exponential, logarithm, square root, and
reversion operations are exercised by
conformance/HexTruncatedSeries/Conformance.lean and by the SymPy fixture oracle
wired through scripts/ci/run_oracles.sh. Conversion and quotient-equivalence
declarations are proofs rather than executable destinations for conformance
cases.
